/s/towmlu","comments_url":"https://lobste.rs/s/towmlu/writing_os_rust_tiny_steps"},{"short_id":"r9jttw","created_at":"2014-03-12T22:46:29.000-05:00","title":"Implementing a web server in a single printf() call","url":"http://tinyhack.com/2014/03/12/implementing-a-web-server-in-a-single-printf-call/","score":3,"flags":0,"comment_count":0,"description":"","description_plain":"","submitter_user":"jm","user_is_author":false,"tags":["c","programming"],"short_id_url":"https://lobste.rs/s/r9jttw","comments_url":"https://lobste.rs/s/r9jttw/implementing_web_server_single_printf"},{"short_id":"advmgj","created_at":"2014-03-12T21:11:50.000-05:00","title":"Samsung Galaxy Back-door","url":"http://redmine.replicant.us/projects/replicant/wiki/SamsungGalaxyBackdoor","score":1,"flags":0,"comment_count":0,"description":"","description_plain":"","submitter_user":"journeysquid","user_is_author":false,"tags":["android","security"],"short_id_url":"https://lobste.rs/s/advmgj","comments_url":"https://lobste.rs/s/advmgj/samsung_galaxy_back_door"},{"short_id":"qtpqju","created_at":"2014-03-12T21:07:59.000-05:00","title":"Attacking the iOS 7 early_random() PRNG","url":"http://blog.azimuthsecurity.com/2014/03/attacking-ios-7-earlyrandom-prng.html","score":4,"flags":0,"comment_count":1,"description":"","description_plain":"","submitter_user":"jcs","user_is_author":false,"tags":["ios","security"],"short_id_url":"https://lobste.rs/s/qtpqju","comments_url":"https://lobste.rs/s/qtpqju/attacking_ios_7_early_random_prng"},{"short_id":"j1yj2n","created_at":"2014-03-12T17:33:42.000-05:00","title":"Consider the Nimrod Programming Language","url":"http://geetduggal.wordpress.com/2014/03/03/consider-nimrod/","score":5,"flags":0,"comment_count":3,"description":"","description_plain":"","submitter_user":"rivd","user_is_author":false,"tags":["programming"],"short_id_url":"https://lobste.rs/s/j1yj2n","comments_url":"https://lobste.rs/s/j1yj2n/consider_nimrod_programming_language"},{"short_id":"csd2tj","created_at":"2014-03-12T17:12:32.000-05:00","title":"A week of no story downvotes","url":"","score":14,"flags":0,"comment_count":17,"description":"\u003cp\u003eIt's been a week since I \u003ca href=\"https://github.com/jcs/lobsters/commit/9535b054907cb80cc78d20badbf4acb462e3ba2a\" rel=\"ugc\"\u003eremoved\u003c/a\u003e story downvoting and replaced it with the hide functionality after some \u003ca href=\"https://lobste.rs/s/qwfnr0/remove_the_low_quality_downvote\" rel=\"ugc\"\u003ediscussion\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eDo you think this has made things better or worse?  I haven't seen any of the after-downvote bickering that I saw before, but I've also heard from users that it's made things worse because low quality articles can't be pulled off the front page anymore.  However, I believe that being able to do that was only temporary because as the site gains more users, the power of one or even a couple downvotes will not be enough to prevent such stories from reaching the front page if enough other users like it.  I would much rather see comments on such stories from users explaining why they don't like it, or engaging the author of the story in a discussion here if he or she has an account.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWhat do you lobsters think?\u003c/p\u003e\n","description_plain":"It's been a week since I [removed](https://github.com/jcs/lobsters/commit/9535b054907cb80cc78d20badbf4acb462e3ba2a) story downvoting and replaced it with the hide functionality after some [discussion](https://lobste.rs/s/qwfnr0/remove_the_low_quality_downvote).\r\n\r\nDo you think this has made things better or worse?  I haven't seen any of the after-downvote bickering that I saw before, but I've also heard from users that it's made things worse because low quality articles can't be pulled off the front page anymore.  However, I believe that being able to do that was only temporary because as the site gains more users, the power of one or even a couple downvotes will not be enough to prevent such stories from reaching the front page if enough other users like it.  I would much rather see comments on such stories from users explaining why they don't like it, or engaging the author of the story in a discussion here if he or she has an account.\r\n\r\nWhat do you lobsters think?","submitter_user":"jcs","user_is_author":false,"tags":["meta"],"short_id_url":"https://lobste.rs/s/csd2tj","comments_url":"https://lobste.rs/s/csd2tj/week_no_story_downvotes"},{"short_id":"ipa83i","created_at":"2014-03-12T17:01:59.000-05:00","title":"Replicant developers find and close Samsung Galaxy back-door","url":"https://www.fsf.org/blogs/community/replicant-developers-find-and-close-samsung-galaxy-backdoor","score":8,"flags":0,"comment_count":6,"description":"","description_plain":"","submitter_user":"jcs","user_is_author":false,"tags":["android","security"],"short_id_url":"https://lobste.rs/s/ipa83i","comments_url":"https://lobste.rs/s/ipa83i/replicant_developers_find_close_samsung"},{"short_id":"w7neue","created_at":"2014-03-12T16:47:51.000-05:00","title":"Guidelines for Setting Security Headers","url":"http://blog.veracode.com/2014/03/guidelines-for-setting-security-headers/","score":5,"flags":0,"comment_count":0,"description":"","description_plain":"","submitter_user":"tedu","user_is_author":false,"tags":["security","web"],"short_id_url":"https://lobste.rs/s/w7neue","comments_url":"https://lobste.rs/s/w7neue/guidelines_for_setting_security_headers"},{"short_id":"9qmmh6","created_at":"2014-03-12T16:42:28.000-05:00","title":"Deep Analysis of CVE-2014-0502 – A Double Free Story","url":"http://blog.spiderlabs.com/2014/03/deep-analysis-of-cve-2014-0502-a-double-free-story.html","score":4,"flags":0,"comment_count":0,"description":"","description_plain":"","submitter_user":"jcs","user_is_author":false,"tags":["reversing","security"],"short_id_url":"https://lobste.rs/s/9qmmh6","comments_url":"https://lobste.rs/s/9qmmh6/deep_analysis_cve_2014_0502_double_free"},{"s